-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 47(d) and the Regulations of 5740-1980. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from the Regulations (lines 16, 19-22) and s 47 (lines
-- 1778-1782) before the rules were run; none edited. The 2026 amounts, as in row IL-08's tests: 2,268; 116,400; 164,400; 165,228 (so the beneficiary member's least
-- sum is 26,436.48).
-- Regulation 2: aged 50 at the start of the tax year, not a beneficiary member. (a)(1) 10.5% of the non-work qualifying income; (a)(2) pension only: a further
-- deduction of the excess over (allowed + 5%), up to 6%; (b) 7.5% of the work qualifying income less insured income. The ceiling of regulation 1:
-- non-work (b)(1): 7% (first rate) or 11% (every rate) of 164,400 = 11,508 or 18,084; work (b)(2): 5% of 116,400 = 5,820.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 47(d) and the Regulations of 5740-1980`

`the 2026 amounts` MEANS `The amounts of sections 45A and 47 in force in the tax year` WITH
    `the amount in section 45A(d)(1)`                                    IS 2268
    `the amount in paragraph (1) of the definition of qualifying income` IS 116400
    `the amount in paragraph (2) of the definition of qualifying income` IS 164400
    `the average wage in the economy, in total for the tax year`         IS 165228

-- An individual in 2026: work income; other income; insured income; deposits; the s 45A pension sums; the s 47 sums under (b).
GIVEN `work`        IS A NUMBER
      `other`       IS A NUMBER
      `insured`     IS A NUMBER
      `deposits`    IS A NUMBER
      `credit sums` IS A NUMBER
      `under (b)`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`R in 2026: work income` `work` `, other income` `other` `, insured income` `insured` `, deposits for him` `deposits` `; for s 45A pension` `credit sums` `; for s 47 under (b)` `under (b)` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS 2026
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS TRUE
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS `work`
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS `other`
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS `other`
        `insured income`                                                                IS `insured`
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS `deposits`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, `credit sums`, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 47` OF `under (b)`, 0, 0, 0
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS 0
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS 0
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS FALSE
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`                                    IS FALSE
        `a foreign worker`                                                                                                  IS FALSE

GIVEN `born`     IS A DATE
      `pension only` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980`
`born` `, paying for a pension only:` `pension only` MEANS
    `An individual's age and kind of payment, for the Regulations of 5740-1980` OF `born`, `pension only`

`aged 56` MEANS YMD 1970 1 1

-- The default readings spelled out: every one declined.
GIVEN `the ceiling`  IS A `A reading of the ceiling of the deduction in regulation 1`
      `the relation` IS A `A reading of regulation 2 against section 47(b)`
GIVETH A `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980`
`the readings: ceiling` `the ceiling` `and relation` `the relation` MEANS
    `The readings of the Regulations of 5740-1980` OF `the ceiling`, `the relation`

§§ `Age: 50 completed years on the first day of the tax year`

-- Self-employed, 100,000 of non-work income, 10,000 paid, not for a pension only, no s 45A sums competing. Ordinary (b): 7% x 100,000 = 7,000 (10,000 is not above 12%).
-- Regulations: (a)(1) 10.5% x 100,000 = 10,500, below the ceiling; the sums paid are 10,000: deduction min(10,000, 10,500) = 10,000. Replace or higher of the two: 10,000.
-- Born 1 January 1976: 50 on 1 January 2026, within. Born 2 January 1976: 49, not within. Born 31 December 1975: 50.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` ((YMD 1976 1 1) `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` ((YMD 1975 12 31) `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` ((YMD 1976 1 2) `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` ((YMD 1990 6 15) `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 7000
#ASSERT `one born on` (YMD 1976 1 1) `has completed 50 years at the start of tax year` 2026 EQUALS TRUE
#ASSERT `one born on` (YMD 1976 1 2) `has completed 50 years at the start of tax year` 2026 EQUALS FALSE

§§ `Fork F12 — the ceiling of regulation 1`

-- 20,000 paid for a pension only; 100,000 of non-work income. (a)(1): 10,500. (a)(2): threshold 10,500 + 5,000 = 15,500; the excess 4,500, within 6% x 100,000 = 6,000: a further 4,500: 15,000.
-- Ceiling: first rate 7% x 164,400 = 11,508; every rate 11% x 164,400 = 18,084. Deduction: first rate min(20,000, 11,508) = 11,508; every rate min(20,000, 15,000) = 15,000.
-- Against s 47(b) (ordinary 7,000 + min(4,000, 8,000) = 11,000): the regulation is higher in both, so replace or higher agree.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` (`the readings: ceiling` `the first rate of the paragraph` `and relation` `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)`) `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 20000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 20000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11508
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` (`the readings: ceiling` `every rate of the paragraph` `and relation` `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)`) `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 20000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 20000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 15000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 20000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 20000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "regulation 1 defines the ceiling of the deduction by the rates fixed in section 47(b)(1) or (2) and does not say whether that is the first rate or every rate of the paragraph, and here the readings differ"
-- Not for a pension only: only (a)(1) is open: 10,500, below both ceilings. The ceiling does not decide; but the relation to s 47(b) does (below).
-- Paying 14,000 for a pension only (a lower sum): the excess over 15,500 is none, so (a)(2) adds nothing: 10,500 under both ceilings; the default (relation: ordinary 7,000 + min(4,000, 2,000) = 9,000 < 10,500) answers.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 14000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 14000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 10500
-- A higher income, where the first rate's ceiling cuts (a)(1) itself: 150,000. (a)(1): 10.5% x 150,000 = 15,750; ceiling 11,508 or 18,084.
-- Paying 15,750 not for a pension only: min(15,750, 11,508) = 11,508 (first rate), min(15,750, 15,750) = 15,750 (every rate). Ordinary: 7% x 150,000 = 10,500 + 0 = 10,500 (15,750 is not above 18,000).
-- Both readings of the relation give the regulation (higher than 10,500). The ceiling decides: declined.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` (`the readings: ceiling` `the first rate of the paragraph` `and relation` `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)`) `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 150000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 15750 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 15750) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11508
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` (`the readings: ceiling` `every rate of the paragraph` `and relation` `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)`) `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 150000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 15750 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 15750) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 15750
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 150000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 15750 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 15750) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "regulation 1 defines the ceiling of the deduction by the rates fixed in section 47(b)(1) or (2) and does not say whether that is the first rate or every rate of the paragraph, and here the readings differ"

§§ `Fork F14 — does the regulation replace s 47(b), or has he the higher?`

-- 100,000 of non-work income, 20,000 paid, NOT for a pension only: (a)(1) alone, 10,500, below both ceilings. Ordinary s 47(b): 11,000.
-- The regulation replaces: 10,500. He has the higher: 11,000. The default declines.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` (`the readings: ceiling` `the first rate of the paragraph` `and relation` `the regulation replaces the rate of section 47(b)`) `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 20000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 20000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 10500
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` (`the readings: ceiling` `the first rate of the paragraph` `and relation` `the individual has the higher of the two`) `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 20000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 20000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 20000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 20000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "the Regulations of 5740-1980 do not say whether the rate they give replaces the rate of section 47(b) or leaves the individual the higher of the two, and here the readings differ"
#ASSERT `the Regulations of 5740-1980 — the readings row IL-27 takes` EQUALS `the readings: ceiling` `declined where the readings differ` `and relation` `declined where the readings differ`

§§ `Regulation 2(b) — an employee`

-- Work income 100,000, none insured, 6,000 paid. Ordinary (b)(2): 5% x 100,000 = 5,000; deduction min(6,000, 5,000) = 5,000.
-- Regulation: 7.5% x 100,000 = 7,500, held to the ceiling 5% x 116,400 = 5,820; deduction min(6,000, 5,820) = 5,820. Higher or replace: 5,820.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 100000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 6000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 6000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 5820
-- Work income 60,000, none insured, 6,000 paid: 7.5% x 60,000 = 4,500 below the ceiling: 4,500 (ordinary 3,000).
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 60000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 6000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 6000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 4500
-- The same under 50: ordinary 5% x 60,000 = 3,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 60000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 6000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 6000) `and` ((YMD 1990 6 15) `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 3000
-- An employee whose whole salary is insured income: nothing, whatever the rate.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 120000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 120000 `, deposits for him` 22200 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 7200) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 0
-- Less than the limit is paid: 2,000 paid by a 60,000 employee: the sums, 2,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 60000 `, other income` 0 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 2000 `; for s 45A pension` 0 `; for s 47 under (b)` 2000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 2000

§§ `A beneficiary member is under (b1), which the Regulations do not touch`

-- Self-employed on 100,000, 30,000 paid for himself under (b1): a beneficiary member (30,000 is at least 26,436.48). (b1)(1): 11% x 100,000 = 11,000, aged 56 or not.
GIVEN `paid` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH AN `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47`
`B in 2026: self-employed on 100,000, paid under (b1)` `paid` MEANS
    `An individual in a tax year, for sections 45A and 47` WITH
        `tax year`                                                                      IS 2026
        `an Israeli resident in the tax year`                                           IS TRUE
        `taxable income from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A`     IS 0
        `taxable income not from work, before the deductions under sections 47 and 47A` IS 100000
        `taxable income from a business or profession`                                  IS 100000
        `insured income`                                                                IS 0
        `sums paid in the tax year to a pension provident fund in respect of the individual's income` IS `paid`
        `sums paid, for section 45A`                                                    IS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 45A` OF 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0
        `sums paid, for section 47`                                                     IS `Sums paid in the tax year, for section 47` OF 0, 0, `paid`, 0
        `sums deducted under section 47(b) or (b1)`                                     IS 0
        `sums deposited to a pension provident fund as a self-employed member for himself, not credited under section 45A(b)` IS 0
        `a deduction was made for him under section 32(14)(b) for preferred insurance against loss of working capacity`      IS FALSE
        `within a class for which regulations under section 47(d) set higher deductions`                                    IS FALSE
        `a foreign worker`                                                                                                  IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`B in 2026: self-employed on 100,000, paid under (b1)` 30000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`B in 2026: self-employed on 100,000, paid under (b1)` 30000) `and` ((YMD 1990 6 15) `, paying for a pension only:` TRUE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 11000

§§ `The order with the s 45A credit (IL-08's fork F35)`

-- 100,000 of non-work income, 10,000 paid, not for a pension only, and the same 10,000 creditable under s 45A. Aged 56: the regulation's deduction first is min(10,000, 10,500) = 10,000.
-- Credit first: s 45A(d)(2)(b)(1) credits 5% x 100,000 = 5,000 (row IL-08, D190), leaving 10,000 - 5,000 = 5,000 for the deduction. The orders differ: declined by default, each by name.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` `the Regulations of 5740-1980 — the readings row IL-27 takes` `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the deduction first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 10000 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` `the Regulations of 5740-1980 — the readings row IL-27 takes` `and the order with the section 45A credit as` `the credit first` `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 10000 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 5000
#ASSERT REFUSED `the deduction under section 47 with the Regulations of 5740-1980 for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 10000 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` BECAUSE "sections 47 and 45A do not say whether the deduction or the credit takes a payment first, and here the order changes the answer"
-- The taxpayer's own choice of order, kept by name: deduction first 10,000; credit first 5,000.
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` `the Regulations of 5740-1980 — the readings row IL-27 takes` `and the order with the section 45A credit as` (`the order the taxpayer chooses` OF TRUE) `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 10000 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 10000
#ASSERT `the deduction under section 47, reading the Regulations of 5740-1980 as` `the Regulations of 5740-1980 — the readings row IL-27 takes` `and the order with the section 45A credit as` (`the order the taxpayer chooses` OF FALSE) `, for` (`R in 2026: work income` 0 `, other income` 100000 `, insured income` 0 `, deposits for him` 10000 `; for s 45A pension` 10000 `; for s 47 under (b)` 10000) `and` (`aged 56` `, paying for a pension only:` FALSE) `, at` `the 2026 amounts` EQUALS 5000

